From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:20:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Describe the CPU cluster power
 gates, disabled

A deep sleep's engine waits for every core to power down, and the boot
CPU only power-gates in WFI if its cluster's enable is set. On T8140
iBoot leaves the P cluster's clear, and the watchdog reset every sleep
until it was set.

The J604's ADT has the window those enables live in on T8140: PMGR
reg[34], PMGR + 0x24000, at the same place in the PMGR block. Which
words in it are the clusters' and what their top bit does is T8140's
layout, not something the ADT says. Describe the node with that layout
and leave it disabled until a read-only probe of both words on the J604
shows it, so that no guessed word is written.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi
index a58b5f2c6d..0132f0aaef 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi
@@ -43,6 +43,20 @@
 	 * CPM gating words (PMGR + 0xc030..) are not known on T8132, and a
 	 * guessed PMGR word is never written.
 	 */
+	/*
+	 * CPU cluster power-gate enables: the J604 ADT's /arm-io/pmgr reg[34]
+	 * (PMGR + 0x24000, size 0x4000), the window that holds them on T8140.
+	 * The words for cluster 0 (E) at +0x0 and 1 (P) at +0x40 and their top
+	 * bit are T8140's layout: TO-VERIFY with a read-only probe of both words
+	 * before this is enabled.
+	 */
+	cluster_pwrgate: power-gate@380724000 {
+		compatible = "apple,t8132-cluster-pwrgate", "apple,cluster-pwrgate";
+		reg = <0x3 0x80724000 0x0 0x4>,
+		      <0x3 0x80724040 0x0 0x4>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+
 	pmgr_sleep: power-management@3882c8000 {
 		compatible = "apple,t8132-pmgr-sleep";
 		reg = <0x3 0x882c8000 0x0 0x1000>,
